# Backend scope

You are working in the Qeeva Django backend. Read `Qeeva-Backend/AGENTS.md` first; it is the full manual.

Key constraints:
- Django 5.2 LTS + Django REST Framework; PostgreSQL on Supabase; Supabase Auth (Django only verifies the JWT, never creates users). No SimpleJWT, no SQLite.
- Django owns the schema: models + migrations only (`RunSQL` for PostgreSQL-specific parts). No changes through the Supabase dashboard.
- Read user data only through `Model.objects.for_user(principal)`; every model declares `OWNER_FIELD`; every table is locked down with `lock_down_table` in its migration.
- Money is integer minor units (`bigint`), never floats.
- No API endpoints beyond `/api/health/` and `/api/me/` until the product owner changes the scope.
- Tests are required. Run from inside `Qeeva-Backend/` (database host `127.0.0.1`, not `localhost`): `docker compose up -d --wait`, set `QEEVA_TEST_DATABASE_URL`, then `python -m pytest`, `ruff check .`, `mypy .`.
- Decisions live in `plans/decisions/decision-log.md`; write new ones in the same commit.
- Never drop/reset a database or touch Supabase without explicit approval.
